      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. if it's PPM or something like that, then the \"stutter\" is actually the data. the more i look at the logs from last night, the more i'm convinced it's addressed to a specific observer. the sequence seems to shift slightly depending on the exact moment i'm tracking it. if we were to try and map the micro-pulse gaps to a binary or a prime number sequence, how would we even start to deconstruct a signal that looks so much like natural scintillation but has this underlying mathematical structure?",
